{
  "info": {
    "_postman_id": "ak-cloud-e2e-saga-positive-v2-2026-07-28",
    "name": "AntKart Cloud E2E Saga - Positive",
    "description": "PAYMENT SUCCESS path end to end against the live AKS platform through https://api.antkart.in.\n\nTOKEN: collection-level OAuth 2.0, Authorization Code with PKCE against Entra ID. Click 'Get New Access Token' on the collection's Authorization tab once per session, complete sign-in and MFA, then 'Use Token'. No token is ever pasted into a variable.\n\nFILL TWO ENVIRONMENT VALUES BEFORE THE FIRST RUN:\n  entraClientId      - the PUBLIC CLIENT app registration id (not the API's id)\n  razorpayKeySecret  - az keyvault secret show --vault-name kv-antkart-dev --name \"Razorpay--KeySecret\" --query value -o tsv\n\nRUN with the Collection Runner, 'Delay between requests' = 8000 ms. The saga is asynchronous; steps 07 and 12 self-retry up to 6 times, which only works in the Runner.\n\nAll request bodies are built in pre-request scripts with JSON.stringify rather than by substituting {{variables}} into raw JSON. Product names in the catalogue can contain double quotes and apostrophes, which break hand-built JSON and produce an empty HTTP 400.\n\nAll paths and payloads come from the service contracts in AntKart-Src3. Only tests executed against cloud resources through https://api.antkart.in are valid.",
    "schema": "https://schema.getpostman.com/json/collection/v2.1.0/collection.json"
  },
